	"Name": "DIYCP Suite",
	"Author": "LavenderLight",
	"AuthorLabel": "Lavender",
	"TagLine": "A do-it-yourself Content Patcher set.",
	"Description": "***PLEASE DO NOT ASK ME ABOUT COMPATIBILITY WITH SVE (STARDEW VALLEY EXPANDED)!!! I DO NOT OFFER SUPPORT FOR IT!***\n\nDIYCP - Do-It-Yourself Content Patcher.\nAll the coding is done for you, just edit the art!\nEdit the sheets yourself, or drag and drop the pngs from other mods in the assets folder (make sure the name is the same and it overwrites!). That's it!\nNow all the mods are included into one easy bundle! Use them all, or delete the ones you're not interested in!\n\n**Another thing since I've seen people ask - you have permission to use DIYCP to learn modding/as a base for your own mods! Just please credit me if you do! :)**\n\n**How To Use:**\n\n1.  [Install the latest version of SMAPI](https://smapi.io/).\n\n2.  [Install Content Patcher](https://www.nexusmods.com/stardewvalley/mods/1915).\n\n3.  Download this mod and unzip it into\u00A0Stardew Valley/Mods.\n\n4.  In this mod's folder, open the assets folder. Edit or replace the pngs with ones of your choice.\n\n5.  Run the game using SMAPI.\n\n6.  That's it!\n**Updates:**\nJanuary 8, 2021:\nUpdated for 1.5 and combined into one mod. :)\n\nDecember 6, 2019:\nI updated all the DIYCPs for 1.4. :)\nJune 24, 2018:\nMade an update log. :')\nI made a config file, which I should had done to begin with. Pardon my laziness! Farmer replacements are set to true (\"yes\") by default, which means it'll load the images to replace stuff like shirts and hairstyles. Set to \"no\" in config, if you use another mod. \"\nCursors/Event NPCs is set to false (\"no\") by default. Set to \"yes\" if you want to use them.\nAdded an update key - SMAPI will now tell you when it updates!",
